@startuml 07-deployment
' ISU Research Study E-Library - Deployment diagram (final, main a7d5ed9)
' Checked against: firebase.json (hosting site isu-elibrary, public dist,
' rewrites to /index.html), src/firebase.ts (getAuth, getFirestore),
' src/extractPdf.ts (Drive API v3 files.get alt=media), src/data.ts,
' firestore.rules, package.json (vite build)
title ISU Research Study E-Library - Deployment (Firebase Spark plan)
skinparam shadowing false

node "User device\n(PC, laptop, tablet or phone)" as Device {
  node "Web browser (Chrome / Edge)" as Browser {
    artifact "React 19 single-page app\n(Vite build: index.html + /assets/*.js, *.css)" as SPA
    component "Firebase JS SDK 12\n(firebase/auth, firebase/firestore)" as SDK
    component "pdf.js (pdfjs-dist) + worker\n(loaded only by Register / Edit)" as PDFJS
    component "In-browser logic:\nBM25F search, Trie + Levenshtein,\nTF-IDF similarity, keyword model,\nextractive summary, APA 7" as Logic
    database "sessionStorage\n(draft, staff view)" as SS
    database "localStorage\n(theme, Forgot password email)" as LS
    SPA ..> SDK
    SPA ..> PDFJS
    SPA ..> Logic
    SPA ..> SS
    SPA ..> LS
  }
}

cloud "Google Firebase (project on the free Spark plan)" as Firebase {
  node "Firebase Hosting\nsite isu-elibrary\n(isu-elibrary.web.app)" as Hosting {
    artifact "dist/ (static files)\nall paths -> /index.html" as Dist
  }
  node "Firebase Authentication" as Auth {
    component "Google provider (pop-up)" as GP
    component "Email/Password provider\n(+ email sign-in links)" as EP
    component "Email sending\n(verification, sign-in link,\nreset email fallback)" as Mailer
  }
  database "Cloud Firestore" as Firestore {
    folder "users" as CUsers
    folder "theses" as CTheses
    artifact "firestore.rules" as Rules
  }
}

cloud "Google APIs" as Google {
  node "Google Drive API v3" as DriveAPI
  storage "Google Drive\n(study PDFs, shared ISU -> Viewer)" as DriveFiles
  DriveAPI -- DriveFiles
}

Browser --> Hosting : HTTPS GET\n(page and JS / CSS assets)
SDK --> "HTTPS\n(sign in, create account,\nsend links, updatePassword)" Auth
SDK --> Firestore : HTTPS (Firestore SDK)\n(onSnapshot, addDoc,\nupdateDoc, deleteDoc, getDoc, setDoc)
SPA --> DriveAPI : HTTPS fetch files.get?alt=media\n(API key restricted to the site addresses)\nonly when no PDF is chosen
Browser --> DriveFiles : Read full study / Open in Drive\n(Google's view-only viewer, new tab)
Rules ..> Auth : checks the ID token\n(email_verified, @isu.edu.ph)

note bottom of Firebase
  No server code, no Cloud Functions, no custom backend.
  All processing (PDF reading, search, similarity,
  keywords, summary) runs in the user's browser.
  Firebase administrator works only in the Firebase console.
end note
@enduml
